 twin son (Gen. 25:25). The name of Edom, “red”, was also given to him from his conduct in connection with the red lentil “pottage” for which he sold his birthright (30, 31).","verses":151,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[34]},{"id":"adah_414","name":"Adah","also":"Bashemath","summary":"The first of Esau’s three wives, the daughter of Elon the Hittite (Gen. 36:2, 4), called also Bashemath (26:34).","verses":6,"father":"Elon","mother":"","v":[34]},{"id":"aholibamah_1761","name":"Aholibamah","also":"Judith","summary":"Jewess, the daughter of Beeri the Hittite, and one of Esau’s wives (Gen. 26:34), elsewhere called Aholibamah (36:2-14).","verses":5,"father":"Beeri","mother":"Anah","v":[34]},{"id":"elon_1182","name":"Elon","also":"","summary":"A Hittite, father of Bashemath, Esau’s wife (Gen. 26:34).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[34]},{"id":"beeri_432","name":"Beeri","also":"","summary":"The father of Judith, one of the wives of Esau (Gen. 26:34), the same as Adah (Gen. 36:2).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[34]}],"places":[{"id":"gerar_459","name":"Gerar","kind":"City","lat":31.38176,"lon":34.60698,"summary":"A region; lodging-place, a very ancient town and district in the south border of Palestine, which was ruled over by a king named Abimelech (Gen. 10:19; 20:1, 2).","verses":9,"v":[1,6,20,26]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[2]},{"id":"valley_of_gerar_1203","name":"valley of Gerar","kind":"Valley","lat":31.39129,"lon":34.56057,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[17]},{"id":"esek_409","name":"Esek","kind":"Landmark (Well)","lat":31.39129,"lon":34.56057,"summary":"Quarrel, a well which Isaac’s herdsmen dug in the valley of Gerar, and so called because the herdsmen of Gerar quarrelled with them for its possession (Gen. 26:20).","v